## Benchmarks in Go

Benchmarks are functions that measure **code performance** — operations per second and memory allocations. Benchmarks live in `_test.go` files and start with `Benchmark`.

## Basic Benchmark Syntax

```go
package stringutil

import "testing"

func BenchmarkReverse(b *testing.B) {
	for i := 0; i < b.N; i++ { // b.N is determined automatically by Go
		Reverse("Hello, Gopher!")
	}
}
```

## Running Benchmarks

```bash
# Run all benchmarks (-bench flag is required)
go test -bench=.

# With memory allocation info
go test -bench=. -benchmem

# Specific benchmark
go test -bench=BenchmarkReverse

# Longer duration for more accurate results
go test -bench=. -benchtime=5s
```

## Benchmark Output

```
BenchmarkReverse-8    	 5000000	       250 ns/op	       32 B/op	        1 allocs/op
│            │          │              │             │              └── allocs per op
│            │          │              │             └──────────────── bytes per op
│            │          │              └────────────────────────────── nanoseconds per op
│            │          └───────────────────────────────────────────── b.N iterations
│            └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── GOMAXPROCS
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── function name
```

## Comparing Implementations

```go
func BenchmarkConcatPlus(b *testing.B) {
	for i := 0; i < b.N; i++ {
		s := ""
		for j := 0; j < 100; j++ {
			s += "x" // slow — creates new string each time
		}
		_ = s
	}
}

func BenchmarkConcatBuilder(b *testing.B) {
	for i := 0; i < b.N; i++ {
		var sb strings.Builder
		for j := 0; j < 100; j++ {
			sb.WriteString("x") // fast — reuses buffer
		}
		_ = sb.String()
	}
}
```

## b.ResetTimer & b.StopTimer

```go
func BenchmarkExpensiveSetup(b *testing.B) {
	// Expensive setup that shouldn't be measured
	data := prepareTestData()

	b.ResetTimer() // start timer from zero
	for i := 0; i < b.N; i++ {
		processData(data)
	}
}

func BenchmarkWithPause(b *testing.B) {
	for i := 0; i < b.N; i++ {
		b.StopTimer()
		cleanup()
		b.StartTimer()
		processData()
	}
}
```

